    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Harrison was initially organized as the Town of Lima in Calumet County back in 1853.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrison_village_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Town of Harrison was officially renamed in 1858, five years after its initial organization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrison_village_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "European immigrants, primarily from Germany, first settled Harrison to farm the fertile lands along Lake Winnebago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrison_village_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Harrison sits on the northeast shore of Lake Winnebago within the Fox Cities metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrison_village_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Niagara Escarpment influences the terrain in Harrison, creating karst landscapes that are prone to sinkholes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harrison_village_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Harrison's early history was defined by an agrarian focus that persisted until suburban expansion began after World War Two.",
